IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cla2-common`
IMPORT `cla2-dust`

-- Civil Liability Act 2002 (WA) -- baseline-2026-11: cases for Part 2 Division 5 (cla2-dust.l4).
-- Edges: each limb of the s 15AB definition; an action started on proclamation day (1 December 2024) and the day before;
-- each s 15AO(3) bar; no later disease named; each s 3A item; each bar on a subsequent action; each limb of s 15AE.
-- Expected values are worked by hand from the deposited text. The facts are illustrative.
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice.

§ `Cases -- dust diseases`

§§ `Short names`

`only dust` MEANS `item 6: inhaling asbestos or silica, and no other item`
`no class` MEANS `none of the s 3A classes`
`CTP` MEANS `item 2: damages the Motor Vehicle (Third Party Insurance) Act 1943 applies to`
`against my employer` MEANS `item 3: a claim against my employer under Part 7 Division 2 of the Workers Compensation and Injury Management Act 2023`
`intentional` MEANS `item 1: an unlawful act intended to cause personal injury, a sexual offence or other unlawful sexual conduct`
`tobacco` MEANS `item 4: smoking or other use of tobacco products`
`air` MEANS `item 5: damages under the Civil Aviation (Carriers' Liability) Act 1961`

§§ `s 15AB -- dust disease`

#ASSERT `Is my condition a dust disease` `the lungs` `pneumoconiosis or silicosis` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my condition a dust disease` `the lungs` `none of the listed diseases` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my condition a dust disease` `the pleura` `none of the listed diseases` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my condition a dust disease` `the peritoneum` `none of the listed diseases` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (b): a listed disease anywhere, for example mesothelioma of the pericardium.
#ASSERT `Is my condition a dust disease` `elsewhere in the body` `mesothelioma` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my condition a dust disease` `elsewhere in the body` `asbestos-induced carcinoma` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Neither (a) nor (b).
#ASSERT `Is my condition a dust disease` `elsewhere in the body` `none of the listed diseases` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Lung cancer from smoking, not dust.
#ASSERT `Is my condition a dust disease` `the lungs` `lung cancer` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 15AC, 15AO, 3A -- provisional damages`

-- Arguments: where; listed disease; from dust; s 3A class; claiming personal injury damages; date commenced; in the Supreme
-- Court; writ nominates provisional damages; later diseases specified; hearing began before 1 Dec 2024; damages or
-- settlement before 1 Dec 2024.
`provisional` MEANS `Can I be awarded provisional damages`

-- A stonemason with silicosis sues in the Supreme Court on proclamation day, nominating provisional damages and naming lung
-- cancer as a later disease.
#ASSERT `provisional` `the lungs` `pneumoconiosis or silicosis` TRUE `only dust` TRUE (Date 1 12 2024) TRUE TRUE 1 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The same on the day before, started in the District Court and amended under s 15AO(2) (then transferred, s 15AO(4)).
#ASSERT `provisional` `the lungs` `pneumoconiosis or silicosis` TRUE `only dust` TRUE (Date 30 11 2024) FALSE TRUE 1 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 15AO(3)(a), (b): too late to amend.
#ASSERT `provisional` `the lungs` `pneumoconiosis or silicosis` TRUE `only dust` TRUE (Date 30 11 2024) TRUE TRUE 1 TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `provisional` `the lungs` `pneumoconiosis or silicosis` TRUE `only dust` TRUE (Date 30 11 2024) TRUE TRUE 1 FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Started after proclamation day outside the Supreme Court (s 15AC(2)).
#ASSERT `provisional` `the lungs` `pneumoconiosis or silicosis` TRUE `only dust` TRUE (Date 3 2 2025) FALSE TRUE 1 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- No later disease specified, or provisional damages not nominated (s 15AC(2)(a), (b)).
#ASSERT `provisional` `the lungs` `pneumoconiosis or silicosis` TRUE `only dust` TRUE (Date 3 2 2025) TRUE TRUE 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `provisional` `the lungs` `pneumoconiosis or silicosis` TRUE `only dust` TRUE (Date 3 2 2025) TRUE FALSE 2 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `provisional` `the pleura` `mesothelioma` TRUE `only dust` TRUE (Date 3 2 2025) TRUE TRUE 2 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The s 3A items: Division 5 kept for items 3 and 6, off for 1, 2, 4 and 5.
#ASSERT `provisional` `the lungs` `asbestosis` TRUE `against my employer` TRUE (Date 3 2 2025) TRUE TRUE 1 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `provisional` `the lungs` `asbestosis` TRUE `no class` TRUE (Date 3 2 2025) TRUE TRUE 1 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `provisional` `the lungs` `asbestosis` TRUE `CTP` TRUE (Date 3 2 2025) TRUE TRUE 1 FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `provisional` `the lungs` `asbestosis` TRUE `intentional` TRUE (Date 3 2 2025) TRUE TRUE 1 FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `provisional` `the lungs` `lung cancer` TRUE `tobacco` TRUE (Date 3 2 2025) TRUE TRUE 1 FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `provisional` `the lungs` `asbestosis` TRUE `air` TRUE (Date 3 2 2025) TRUE TRUE 1 FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not a dust disease; not a claim for personal injury damages.
#ASSERT `provisional` `the lungs` `lung cancer` FALSE `only dust` TRUE (Date 3 2 2025) TRUE TRUE 1 FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `provisional` `the lungs` `asbestosis` TRUE `only dust` FALSE (Date 3 2 2025) TRUE TRUE 1 FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `ss 15AG, 15AJ -- a subsequent action`

-- Arguments: s 3A class; named in the first writ; already the subject of a subsequent action; how the initial action ended;
-- another subsequent action settled with a bar.
`subsequent` MEANS `Can I bring a subsequent action for a later dust disease`
`not settled` MEANS `it was not settled in whole by a settlement agreement`
`settled, free` MEANS `settled in whole; the agreement says I am not barred from a subsequent action for this disease`
`settled, other barred` MEANS `settled in whole; the agreement bars a subsequent action for some other disease but not this one`
`settled, barred` MEANS `settled in whole; the agreement says I am barred from a subsequent action for this disease`

#ASSERT `subsequent` `only dust` TRUE FALSE `not settled` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `subsequent` `only dust` TRUE FALSE `settled, free` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 15AG(3): not named in the first writ.
#ASSERT `subsequent` `only dust` FALSE FALSE `not settled` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 15AG(5), s 15AJ: already sued for.
#ASSERT `subsequent` `only dust` TRUE TRUE `not settled` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 15AG(6)(a), (b).
#ASSERT `subsequent` `only dust` TRUE FALSE `settled, barred` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `subsequent` `only dust` TRUE FALSE `settled, free` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Fork F4: a bar on another disease only.
#ASSERT `subsequent` `only dust` TRUE FALSE `settled, other barred` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `subsequent` `against my employer` TRUE FALSE `not settled` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `subsequent` `CTP` TRUE FALSE `not settled` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `ss 15AE, 15AL -- the settlement agreement`

-- Arguments: lists every later disease; how many it lists; says whether liability is admitted for the disease settled; for
-- each later disease; says whether I am barred.
`agreement` MEANS `Does my settlement agreement say what the Act requires`

#ASSERT `agreement` TRUE 1 TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Fork F6: none listed, so (b)(ii) and (c) have nothing to bite on.
#ASSERT `agreement` TRUE 0 TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `agreement` TRUE 2 TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `agreement` TRUE 2 TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `agreement` FALSE 0 TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `agreement` TRUE 1 FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 15AF, 15AM -- a settled action`

#ASSERT `What happens to my settled dust disease action` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `it must be discontinued, which keeps a further action open`
#ASSERT `What happens to my settled dust disease action` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `it may be dismissed`
#ASSERT `What happens to my settled dust disease action` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Act does not say`
-- Both: the agreement leaves a listed disease open that the writ did not name, and bars all the writ's. "must be
-- discontinued" governs.
#ASSERT `What happens to my settled dust disease action` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `it must be discontinued, which keeps a further action open`

§§ `s 15AK -- earlier amounts`

#ASSERT `What earlier amounts count against my subsequent damages` 100000 50000 20000 EQUALS 170000
#ASSERT `What earlier amounts count against my subsequent damages` 0 0 0 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `What earlier amounts count against my subsequent damages` 0 0 350000 EQUALS 350000
